course: dictionary
lesson: 10617
title: Unexpected things
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word unexpected is made of three parts: un- (not), expect (to think something will happen) and -ed. So unexpected means not expected, something that surprises you because you did not think it would happen. «A self-checkout scanner complains about an unexpected item in the bagging area.» The machine did not expect that item there, so it reacts.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «An unexpected visitor knocked on the door.» The clue is that the visitor was not planned. Swap in your meaning: «a not-expected visitor knocked on the door» still makes sense, so you have got it.
explain: Unexpected can change into other forms. Unexpectedly is an adverb, as in «The bus stopped unexpectedly.» The unexpected is a noun, as in the phrase «Expect the unexpected», which means be ready for surprises.
fact: Unexpected means not expected; surprising because you did not think it would happen.
fact: Unexpectedly means in a way that nobody thought would happen.
fact: The unexpected means surprising things, as in «Expect the unexpected».
fact: «An emergency fund is money kept for unexpected costs», so a sudden repair can be paid for from it.
fact: The prefix un- often means "not", as in unkind, unhappy and unsafe.
exercise: «An unexpected visitor knocked on the door.» What does unexpected mean? | Very loud and noisy | Hungry and tired | Expected for weeks and marked on the calendar | *Not expected, a surprise
exercise: Which part of the word unexpected means "not"? | *un- | -ed | ex- | -pect
exercise: «Expect the unexpected» means | Never leave the house | Only expect good things to happen | *Be ready for surprises | Stop expecting anything at all
test: «The bus stopped unexpectedly, and we all fell forward.» What does unexpectedly mean here? | Very loudly | *In a surprising way, when nobody expected it | On time, exactly as planned | Slowly and carefully, with a long pause
test: «An emergency fund is money kept for unexpected costs.» What are unexpected costs? | Costs that are always the same every month | Costs nobody planned for | *Costs that nobody planned for | Costs paid only by the bank
exam: «Games taught some unexpected things.» In this sentence, what does unexpected tell you about the things? | They were paid for in advance | They were old and very dusty | *They were surprising | They were needed every day
